(912113, 103478, 23412, '<td valign="top">The egg idea is pretty good.  The colors reflecting off the CD, however, give the impression that something unintended is going on with your optics.  The background also takes away a clean line from the edge of the egg, so it appears to be a bit too soft on the focus in that area.  IMO, the shot of the egg shell would have done quite a bit better had it not be on that CD.  Good first entry, though!</td>', 'The egg idea is pretty good.  The colors reflecting off the CD, however, give the impression that something unintended is going on with your optics.  The background also takes away a clean line from the edge of the egg, so it appears to be a bit too soft on the focus in that area.  IMO, the shot of the egg shell would have done quite a bit better had it not be on that CD.  Good first entry, though!', '2004-09-15 20:09:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(912156, 103725, 3214, '<td valign="top">Thanks!  Agreed, the hill works;  we get nice early evening light, so it''s easy to get the "catchlight" in their eyes.  I shoot shutter priority and am constantly switching speeds (and ISO) as the shadows deepen--my models don''t follow direction very well and relocate on a whim.<br/> <br/>This image was pretty much out of the camera except a little Dfine for noise reduction/levels/a bit of saturation, USM@50%, then toning.  <br/> <br/>Am delighted at the top ten finish, thanks for all the comments too!</td>', 'Thanks!  Agreed, the hill works;  we get nice early evening light, so it''s easy to get the "catchlight" in their eyes.  I shoot shutter priority and am constantly switching speeds (and ISO) as the shadows deepen--my models don''t follow direction very well and relocate on a whim. This image was pretty much out of the camera except a little Dfine for noise reduction/levels/a bit of saturation, USM@50%, then toning.   Am delighted at the top ten finish, thanks for all the comments too!', '2004-09-15 20:40:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(912252, 102609, 23478, '<td valign="top">Let me be frank, you have an excellent photo here.  I am not sure why there are only three comments and you finished 192nd.  I always look for interesting subject matter and this is truly amazing.  I gave it a 9 and think that this shot easily should have finished in the top 20.  Well done.</td>', 'Let me be frank, you have an excellent photo here.  I am not sure why there are only three comments and you finished 192nd.  I always look for interesting subject matter and this is truly amazing.  I gave it a 9 and think that this shot easily should have finished in the top 20.  Well done.', '2004-09-15 22:07:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(912262, 102271, 3280, '<td valign="top">I''m very dissapointed that this shot didn''t do better.  I agree that it was a lot better than the flower shots.  Good eye and keep up the great work!</td>', 'I''m very dissapointed that this shot didn''t do better.  I agree that it was a lot better than the flower shots.  Good eye and keep up the great work!', '2004-09-15 22:17:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(912294, 103283, 21069, '<td valign="top">Thanks everyone who made a comment - hope i place better in my next challenge -- hard to do worst, lol</td>', 'Thanks everyone who made a comment - hope i place better in my next challenge -- hard to do worst, lol', '2004-09-15 22:40:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(912298, 103980, 10390, '<td valign="top">Thanks guys. I really didn''t expect it to be higher, this isn''t a photo that is likely to be voted very high in average here on dpc.  I think you have to take a good look at it and then its strength will grow on you and you will then learn to appreciate it more.  A quick look, as it is often when voting in the challenges, doesn''t work for this image.  I knew that when I submitted it and that it didn''t get a higher avg vote was expected.  As I mentioned in the photographer''s comment here above, when I submitted the photo, I was just interested in people''s opinions.  I''m just glad it ended above 5.<br/> <br/>At least all of the comments were positive, many thanks for all your comments.<br/>-.clic</td>', 'Thanks guys. I really didn''t expect it to be higher, this isn''t a photo that is likely to be voted very high in average here on dpc.  I think you have to take a good look at it and then its strength will grow on you and you will then learn to appreciate it more.  A quick look, as it is often when voting in the challenges, doesn''t work for this image.  I knew that when I submitted it and that it didn''t get a higher avg vote was expected.  As I mentioned in the photographer''s comment here above, when I submitted the photo, I was just interested in people''s opinions.  I''m just glad it ended above 5. At least all of the comments were positive, many thanks for all your comments.-.clic', '2004-09-15 22:47:43.000000', NULL, 0),
