(915400, 103935, 26823, '<td valign="top">what a great idea; this is great!</td>', 'what a great idea; this is great!', '2004-09-18 01:28:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(915644, 102794, 10634, '<td valign="top">"For backlighting, I resurrected two old Honeywell Strobonar 200''s - one aimed into the back of the lantern from just below the covered stool on which I placed the lantern."<br/> <br/>I''d like to see what you would get with just this lighting. Eliminating the front lighting which far overpowered the back would make for a far more effective backlighting photo. Otherwise, because it was such a quality photo to begin with I gave you a 7. Had this been in a still life challenge, you would have gotten a 10 from me. <br/> <br/></td>', '"For backlighting, I resurrected two old Honeywell Strobonar 200''s - one aimed into the back of the lantern from just below the covered stool on which I placed the lantern." I''d like to see what you would get with just this lighting. Eliminating the front lighting which far overpowered the back would make for a far more effective backlighting photo. Otherwise, because it was such a quality photo to begin with I gave you a 7. Had this been in a still life challenge, you would have gotten a 10 from me.  ', '2004-09-18 08:28:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(915650, 102761, 4482, '<td valign="top">Awsome shot Eric!! GO team Nikon!!! :P</td>', 'Awsome shot Eric!! GO team Nikon!!! :P', '2004-09-18 08:34:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(915758, 102645, 25553, '<td valign="top">did you try a close up on the fountain on the far right? It looks like it would be very interesting for its color and shape. And people will definetly see that it is backlit. nice pic though</td>', 'did you try a close up on the fountain on the far right? It looks like it would be very interesting for its color and shape. And people will definetly see that it is backlit. nice pic though', '2004-09-18 12:50:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(915772, 102645, 23338, '<td valign="top">Pearcer, I wasn''t one of those 1, 2, or 3 raters.  I was sorta middle of the road (5).  The trouble I have with these type of photos is that they lack a central subject; there are lots of subjects in them and you aren''t really sure what to concentrate on.  I did see backlighting, so I was ok there.  I just didn''t see a real, standout, ''knock you dead'' kind of subject.  It was nicely photographed, it just lacked that big punch that a challenge winner needs.  Hope that helps.  By the way, just because you weren''t able to get something that scored really well doesn''t mean that all the rest of us were able to do so.  (Obviously!)  You are in good company.</td>', 'Pearcer, I wasn''t one of those 1, 2, or 3 raters.  I was sorta middle of the road (5).  The trouble I have with these type of photos is that they lack a central subject; there are lots of subjects in them and you aren''t really sure what to concentrate on.  I did see backlighting, so I was ok there.  I just didn''t see a real, standout, ''knock you dead'' kind of subject.  It was nicely photographed, it just lacked that big punch that a challenge winner needs.  Hope that helps.  By the way, just because you weren''t able to get something that scored really well doesn''t mean that all the rest of us were able to do so.  (Obviously!)  You are in good company.', '2004-09-18 13:07:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(915794, 103455, 5728, '<td valign="top">Critique Club here:<br/> <br/>Hey Peter! I am doing one of my very rare appearances as a member of the critique club, actually I think this only my second or third time this year :) A very strong photo and submission to the backlighting challenge. In my opinion it should have placed a lot higher in the challenge, but you know how it is with flower shots and DPC :) There is not much really I can add to the comments you''ve already received, saying that there is not much to critisize about at all. The orange/yellow color tones work very well in conjunction with the black background and the backlighting set-up brings out those colors fantastically. The soft feel to the whole image brings in a mellow effect which I like, however the more softness you bring into a photo always brings on a decrease in detail and sharpness, so it is a very fine balance one has to take into account. I personally think there may be just a tad too much softness in this image, I would have liked to have seen just a tiny bit more detail in the petals. I am also wondering why you used ISO 1600 for this shot, did you forget to reset the camera?<br/>All in all a shot you can be very proud of and congratulations on your 21st placing.</td>', 'Critique Club here: Hey Peter! I am doing one of my very rare appearances as a member of the critique club, actually I think this only my second or third time this year :) A very strong photo and submission to the backlighting challenge. In my opinion it should have placed a lot higher in the challenge, but you know how it is with flower shots and DPC :) There is not much really I can add to the comments you''ve already received, saying that there is not much to critisize about at all. The orange/yellow color tones work very well in conjunction with the black background and the backlighting set-up brings out those colors fantastically. The soft feel to the whole image brings in a mellow effect which I like, however the more softness you bring into a photo always brings on a decrease in detail and sharpness, so it is a very fine balance one has to take into account. I personally think there may be just a tad too much softness in this image, I would have liked to have seen just a tiny bit more detail in the petals. I am also wondering why you used ISO 1600 for this shot, did you forget to reset the camera?All in all a shot you can be very proud of and congratulations on your 21st placing.', '2004-09-18 13:36:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(915906, 103455, 22781, '<td valign="top">Thanx for your CC comment Gary,<br/> <br/>As of this week I''ve become a CC member myself, and I know how much time and effort goes into it.<br/> <br/>I appreciate it, especially coming from you. <br/></td>', 'Thanx for your CC comment Gary, As of this week I''ve become a CC member myself, and I know how much time and effort goes into it. I appreciate it, especially coming from you. ', '2004-09-18 15:49:26.000000', NULL, 0),
