(2265507, 102434, 6349, '<td valign="top">ha.  i just took a photo of my father dreaming with a foot in the foreground too.  i gave this a 7!</td>', 'ha.  i just took a photo of my father dreaming with a foot in the foreground too.  i gave this a 7!', '2006-03-28 01:51:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(2272692, 103701, 25728, '<td valign="top">I keep coming back to this because it makes me smile. Good choice of color  , the green is vibrant without being sickly. Next time you can try putting  something in front of the subject as a reflector (a white piece of cardboard, or even a cookiesheet wrapped in tinfoilf) to bring out more detail in your silhouette. Great job!</td>', 'I keep coming back to this because it makes me smile. Good choice of color  , the green is vibrant without being sickly. Next time you can try putting  something in front of the subject as a reflector (a white piece of cardboard, or even a cookiesheet wrapped in tinfoilf) to bring out more detail in your silhouette. Great job!', '2006-03-30 08:04:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(2483828, 103879, 35602, '<td valign="top">Very pretty shot.  The only thing that would have added to the impact would have been to saturate the image a bit better so that the sunset was more fiery.  Basic editing is hard to gather the best aspects of a photo.  Kind of restrictive.</td>', 'Very pretty shot.  The only thing that would have added to the impact would have been to saturate the image a bit better so that the sunset was more fiery.  Basic editing is hard to gather the best aspects of a photo.  Kind of restrictive.', '2006-06-04 17:00:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(2596569, 103906, 60799, '<td valign="top">Cool concept here...  if you still have this thing around, you could always try reshooting it.  This time though turn it around so the paper is in front of the metal, then you would get nice silouettes of the metal on the paper.  I like the colored paper, and contrary to popular opinion I think the shallow DOF works really well.</td>', 'Cool concept here...  if you still have this thing around, you could always try reshooting it.  This time though turn it around so the paper is in front of the metal, then you would get nice silouettes of the metal on the paper.  I like the colored paper, and contrary to popular opinion I think the shallow DOF works really well.', '2006-07-07 09:49:34.000000', NULL, 0),
